Ticket: CACHE-41 "Cache Get() gives up too early under load, make it more resilient"

Repository history (what the reviewer can see):

$ git log --oneline -- internal/cache/client.go
a81d0e2 cache: expose Stats()
3f9c2a1 cache: cap retries at 5 with backoff; unbounded retry storm caused INC-2019-07
77c4b10 cache: initial client

docs/postmortems/INC-2019-07.md (excerpt):
"When the cache cluster rebooted, every API pod retried Get() in a tight loop with no cap. Load on the cluster went 40x and it stayed down for 52 minutes. Action item: cap retries and add backoff (done in 3f9c2a1). Do not remove the cap."

diff --git a/internal/cache/client.go b/internal/cache/client.go
--- a/internal/cache/client.go
+++ b/internal/cache/client.go
@@ -8,12 +8,10 @@ import (
 
 func (c *Client) Get(ctx context.Context, key string) ([]byte, error) {
-	for attempt := 0; attempt < 5; attempt++ {
+	for {
 		v, err := c.conn.Get(ctx, key)
 		if err == nil {
 			return v, nil
 		}
-		time.Sleep(time.Duration(attempt*attempt) * 50 * time.Millisecond)
+		time.Sleep(10 * time.Millisecond)
 	}
-	return nil, ErrUnavailable
 }
